<%--
Parent_Selector_Input

Composite form input for a task's polymorphic parent (taskable). A type <select>
(None / Task / Project / Client / User) drives a nested Ajax_Entity_Select_Input
that searches the chosen entity type via Frontend_Tasks_Controller.search_parents.
Changing the type reloads the entity options (and clears the current selection).

val() get/set is `{type: 'Project_Model'|null, id: int|null}` and is
timing-indifferent per the Form_Input_Abstract contract (the base buffers a
pre-ready val() and applies it at _mark_ready). Fires 'input' (user changes only)
and 'val' (all changes) with the {type,id} object.

Flat submission: two mirror hidden inputs (name="taskable_type"/"taskable_id")
carry the value to the controller in the SAME flat shape it already reads -
Rsx_Form.vals() collects hidden [name] inputs directly, so no controller change is
needed. The composite's own val() (the {type,id} object) rides under its $name and
is ignored by the controller.

$exclude_id - a task id whose subtree is excluded from Task-type options (edit
              mode passes the task's own id to prevent a circular chain).
--%>
<Define:Parent_Selector_Input>
    <select $sid="type" class="form-select Parent_Selector_Input__type">
        <option value="None">No parent</option>
        <option value="Task_Model">Task</option>
        <option value="Project_Model">Project</option>
        <option value="Client_Model">Client</option>
        <option value="User_Model">User</option>
    </select>

    <div $sid="entity_wrap" class="Parent_Selector_Input__entity">
        <Ajax_Entity_Select_Input $sid="entity" $parent_type="Project_Model" $placeholder="Search for a parent..." />
    </div>

    <input type="hidden" $sid="h_type" name="taskable_type" />
    <input type="hidden" $sid="h_id" name="taskable_id" />
</Define:Parent_Selector_Input>
